# assets/hero.tape.in — the ONE hand-authored body behind every repo's README hero.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE. The tapes are GENERATED from it by
# scripts/gen-hero-tape.sh, one per row of assets/hero-repos.txt, and
# audit-core.sh §9j reds if a rendered tape drifts from this template.
# Edit HERE, then run `make gen-hero-tape`.
#
# WHY A TEMPLATE. assets/README.md already claimed the property that makes this
# possible — "re-run the command after any prompt or tooling change and the hero
# updates, no manual re-recording" — and then the fleet had exactly one hero, shot
# inside the wrong repo (#698). Nine hand-recorded gifs would drift the way the
# theme (#679), the alias tables (#685) and the porting matrix (#686) drifted; the
# per-repo delta here is two lines, so it is a substitution, not nine files.
#
# PLACEHOLDERS, substituted by the generator. Everything else is verbatim:
#   @@HEADER@@    the generated-file provenance banner
#   @@THEME@@     `Set Theme { … }`, rendered from theme/palette.toml
#   @@CHECKOUT@@  the repo's checkout path — the `cd` in the hidden setup
#   @@SIGCMD@@    the ONE command that is this repo's own (Core: `core status`;
#                 an OS repo: `up -n`, which resolves to that distro's manager)
#   @@SIGNOTE@@   the trailing comment on that line — a TAPE comment, never in the gif
#   @@PROOF@@     the line that makes the resolution VISIBLE: `up -n` prints "via zypper",
#                 the manager and not the verb, so it alone cannot show `dup` rather than
#                 `up` — the distinction #698 is about. This prints the resolved command.
#
# KEEP IT SHORT — the budget is ~15 s, and it is a real budget: §9k caps the
# rendered gif's bytes, and every Sleep here is paid for in that file.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@@HEADER@@

Output assets/demo.gif

Set Shell "zsh"
Set FontFamily "JetBrainsMono Nerd Font"   # must be a Nerd Font, or icons break
Set FontSize 20
Set Width 1200
Set Height 700
Set Padding 20
@@THEME@@
Set TypingSpeed 45ms

# --- silent setup: land on a clean prompt, with nothing that can page ---
# CORE_NO_PAGER and GIT_PAGER are what let the tour drop the four `q` keystrokes
# the first cut needed: a pager costs a Type, an Enter and two Sleeps per command,
# which is most of the difference between a ~27 s clip and this one.
#
# `|| exit 1` ON THE cd IS LOAD-BEARING. This block is hidden, so a `cd` to a path that
# does not exist on the rendering box prints its error into frames nobody records and
# then films $HOME — a hero of the wrong tree, which is #698's original defect wearing a
# different hat. Exiting kills the session instead, so vhs fails visibly rather than
# producing a plausible-looking gif of the wrong directory.
Hide
Type "export CORE_NO_PAGER=1 GIT_PAGER=cat" Enter
Type "source ~/.config/zsh/.zshrc" Enter
Type "cd @@CHECKOUT@@ || exit 1" Enter
Type "clear" Enter
Show
Sleep 1500ms

# --- the tour: three shared marquee moments, then the two that are this repo's ---
Type "ll" Sleep 400ms Enter Sleep 1600ms             # eza — icons + git status
Type "cat README.md" Sleep 400ms Enter Sleep 1600ms  # bat — syntax highlighting
Type "glog -8" Sleep 400ms Enter Sleep 1600ms        # git log, graphed and decorated
Type "@@SIGCMD@@" Sleep 400ms Enter Sleep 2200ms  # @@SIGNOTE@@
Type "@@PROOF@@" Sleep 400ms Enter Sleep 2200ms
Sleep 1s
